<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Warren Hastings</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1732">1732</a>–<a href="/years/1818">1818</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Warren Hastings was the first Governor-General of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>, heading the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a>'s administration in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> from 1773 to 1785. He reorganised revenue and justice, fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mysore">Mysore</a>, and patronised oriental learning. On his return to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> he was impeached for corruption, and acquitted in 1795 after a seven-year trial.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/warren-hastings.jpg" alt="Warren Hastings" width="320" height="402" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sir Joshua Reynolds · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Warren_Hastings_by_Sir_Joshua_Reynolds.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
